course: dictionary
lesson: 2177
title: Old words for pirates
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A corsair is an old word for a pirate, especially one from North Africa who attacked ships in the Mediterranean Sea. You can find the meaning in the sentence itself. «A field-mouse who was captured at sea by a Barbary corsair (a pirate from North Africa)» gives you the answer in the brackets.
explain: The other clues point the same way. The corsair captured the mouse at sea, and the mouse had to row. Ships, the sea and capturing people all belong to a pirate story. To check, swap pirate into the sentence: «captured at sea by a Barbary pirate» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Corsair can also mean the pirate ship itself. Pirate stories use the word for a dashing pirate, a bold and daring one. Because it is an old word, you will mostly meet it in history books, sea stories and tales like The Wind in the Willows.
fact: A corsair is a pirate, especially one from North Africa.
fact: Barbary corsairs attacked ships in the Mediterranean Sea.
fact: A corsair can also mean a pirate ship.
fact: «Corsair» is an old word, so you will mostly find it in history and sea stories.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Sea Rat tells of his voyages in the Mediterranean, a sea once full of corsairs.
exercise: «A Barbary corsair captured the ship at sea.» What is a corsair? | A sailor who rows boats for a living | A kind of fish that lives in the Mediterranean | A castle by the sea | *A pirate, especially one from North Africa
exercise: In «a Barbary corsair (a pirate from North Africa)», which words tell you what a corsair is? | a convent | a lady-love | a field-mouse | *a pirate from North Africa
exercise: Corsair can also mean what? | A long rope for tying boats | A bird that sings over the sea | *A pirate ship | A kind of seashell
test: In The Wind in the Willows, the Sea Rat tells of voyages in a sea full of corsairs. Which sea is it? | The North Pole | A small pond in the park | The Atlantic | *The Mediterranean
test: Pirate stories use «corsair» for which kind of pirate? | A pirate who is afraid of the sea | A teacher who works on a school ship | *A dashing, bold pirate | A sleepy farmer who never leaves home
exam: What is the best check for the meaning of a new word? | Skip the sentence and never look back | Count the letters in the word | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Read only the title of the story
